{
  "category": "recent_news",
  "goals": [
    {
      "id": "recent_news-01",
      "goal": "What changed in Rust 1.99.0?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "Rust 1.99.0 was announced on Oct. 1, 2026 by the Rust Release Team.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rust 1.99.0 stabilizes defining C-ABI variadic functions (using `...`) in Rust itself.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The C-variadic functions stabilized in Rust 1.99.0 can use the \"C\" and \"C-unwind\" ABIs.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The type of `...` in a C-variadic function is `VaList` (`core::ffi::VaList`).",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "`VaList` is ABI-compatible with the C `va_list` type across targets.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rust 1.99.0 stabilizes `Layout::for_value_raw`, which gets the layout of a value behind a raw pointer, including non-Sized types.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rust 1.99.0 stabilizes `mem::size_of_val_raw` for getting the size of a value behind a raw pointer.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rust 1.99.0 stabilizes `mem::align_of_val_raw` for getting the alignment of a value behind a raw pointer.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The `Box::leak` documentation now recommends against patterns that later deallocate the leaked memory.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The `Box::leak` documentation says `Box::into_non_null` or `Box::into_raw` should be preferred over round-trip unleaking.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/01/Rust-1.99.0/",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-02",
      "goal": "What is the Rust project's announced change for the i686 Windows targets coming with Rust 1.100.0?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "The i686 Windows target changes take effect with Rust 1.100.0.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The change was announced on the Rust blog on Oct. 2, 2026.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "`i686-pc-windows-msvc` is demoted from Tier 1 with host tools to Tier 1 without host tools.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "`i686-pc-windows-gnu` is demoted from Tier 2 with host tools to Tier 2 without host tools.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Host tools such as the compiler will no longer be available for these targets.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Builds of the standard library will continue to be distributed for these targets.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Building 32-bit Windows binaries will require cross-compiling from a still-supported host such as 64-bit Windows.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "RFC 3999 covers the `i686-pc-windows-msvc` demotion.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "MCP 1020 covers the `i686-pc-windows-gnu` demotion.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/10/02/demoting-i686-windows-targets-to-std-only/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-03",
      "goal": "What was the Rust security team's September 2026 advisory about Miri and GitHub Actions caching, and how should affected projects respond?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "Miri stores all environment variables to the `target/` directory.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Secrets in the environment can persist in caches of `target/`.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "When paired with GitHub Actions caching that PR CI runs can read, this can expose secrets to PRs.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anyone who has previously landed a change can trigger a PR CI run that extracts information from the cached `target/`.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The short-term fix makes Miri preserve only `CARGO_*` environment variables (excepting `CARGO_*_TOKEN`) and `OUT_DIR`.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Miri release in the nightly of 2026-09-22 no longer has this problem.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "A recommended quick fix is to disable the cache for the job that runs Miri.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "A recommended quick fix is to scope secrets to steps in that job that do not call Miri.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "After applying a fix, projects should clear the cache.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Projects should consider rotating any secrets that might have leaked.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/09/21/github-actions-leaking-secrets-when-miri-output-is-cached/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-04",
      "goal": "What are the main language and tooling changes in Go 1.27?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "Go 1.27 was released on 19 August 2026.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://go.dev/blog/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Go 1.27 supports generic methods: a method declaration may declare its own type parameters.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Interface methods may not declare type parameters in Go 1.27.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "A key in a struct literal may now be any valid field selector for the struct type, not just a top-level field name.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Function type inference is generalized to apply in all contexts where a generic function is assigned to a matching function type.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "`go doc` now supports the `package@version` syntax.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "For modules declaring go 1.27 or later, `go mod tidy` merges duplicate require blocks into at most two blocks: direct and indirect dependencies.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The go command no longer supports the `bzr` version control system.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "`go fix` includes new modernizers: `atomictypes`, `embedlit`, `slicesbackward` and `unsafefuncs`.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "`go test` now runs the `stdversion` vet check by default.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://go.dev/doc/go1.27",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-05",
      "goal": "What are the headline features of Python 3.15, and when is 3.15.0 final due?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "PEP 810 adds explicit lazy imports through a new `lazy` soft keyword.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "A lazy import defers loading the module until the imported name is first used.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15 adds a `frozendict` built-in type (PEP 814).",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15 adds a `sentinel` built-in type (PEP 661).",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15 uses UTF-8 as the default encoding (PEP 686).",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15 adds unpacking in comprehensions.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15 adds a stable ABI for free-threaded builds.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15 adds a dedicated `profiling` package (PEP 799).",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The `profiling` package includes Tachyon, a high-frequency statistical sampling profiler.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://docs.python.org/3.15/whatsnew/3.15.html",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Python 3.15.0 final is scheduled for 2026-10-09.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://blog.python.org/2026/10/python-3150-rc3/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "3.15.0rc3 was released on Oct. 2, 2026 as a surprise extra release candidate.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://www.python.org/downloads/release/python-3150rc3/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-06",
      "goal": "What was in the PostgreSQL 19 Beta 4 release and which features were reverted?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "PostgreSQL 19 Beta 4 was released on September 24, 2026.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 reverts SQL/PGQ (property graph query) support.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 reverts online enabling and disabling of data checksums.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 reverts temporal update/delete support provided by the `FOR PORTION OF` clause.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 reverts `ALTER TABLE ... MERGE PARTITIONS`.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 reverts `ALTER TABLE ... SPLIT PARTITIONS`.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 removes the `pg_get_role_ddl()`, `pg_get_tablespace_ddl()` and `pg_get_database_ddl()` functions.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Beta 4 includes several fixes for the new `REPACK` command.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The next planned PostgreSQL 19 release is the release candidate, expected in early October.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "PostgreSQL 19 GA may also occur in October.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://www.postgresql.org/about/news/postgresql-19-beta-4-released-3386/",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-07",
      "goal": "What's new in Kubernetes v1.37?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "Kubernetes v1.37 was announced on August 26, 2026.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The release theme of Kubernetes v1.37 is \"Garhwal\".",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kubernetes v1.37 consists of 67 enhancements.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "HorizontalPodAutoscaler scale to zero graduates to Beta and is enabled by default.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "HorizontalPodAutoscaler scale to zero is applied by setting `spec.minReplicas: 0`.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "HorizontalPodAutoscaler scale to zero applies to workloads that use object or external metrics.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Manifest-based admission control configuration graduates to Beta.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Admission webhooks and CEL-based policies are loaded from manifest files on disk via the `staticManifestsDir` field in `AdmissionConfiguration`.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pod-level checkpoint and restore is introduced as an Alpha feature.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pod-level checkpoint and restore extends the CRI with `CheckpointPod` and `RestorePod` RPCs.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release",
          "volatility": "slow",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "recent_news-08",
      "goal": "What notable features were added in Node.js 26.10.0?",
      "nuggets": [
        {
          "text": "Node.js 26.10.0 (Current) was released on 2026-09-22.",
          "scope": "supporting",
          "url": "https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.10.0",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Node.js 26.10.0 adds `crypto.parsePKCS12()`.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.10.0",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Node.js 26.10.0 adds `util.throttle`.",
          "scope": "core",
          "url": "https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.10.0",
          "volatility": "fast",
          "verified_on": "2026-10-08"
        },
